      "writtenOn": "2021-08-10T22:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Well, for one, ioctl() has always reported error here, so to do otherwise would be a breaking change. (As in, the Thou Shalt Not Break User Space kind.)\n\nActually: I\u0027m lost. There are no specific references here about what exactly broke -- did anyone bisect (or similar) and point at a specific commit? IIUC, it\u0027s this commit that was the problem:\n\nhttps://git.kernel.org/linus/413dda8f2c6f1ba90e93ba7b4214b1d8cf8ec171\nplatform/chrome: cros_ec_chardev: Use cros_ec_cmd_xfer_status helper\n\nSo the simple answer is that we should go back to that behavior, which involves undoing a few things to reintroduce the cros_ec_cmd_xfer() helper.",
      "parentUuid": "1dea8387_9a73271a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 202,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3ccd1b2f34b5769eafb1b489e9cb6ea9edf728da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3bd69a0_6fd96970",
        "filename": "util/comm-dev.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-13T14:51:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also don\u0027t own any of the patches involved here and I don\u0027t have kernel experience, so I don\u0027t have a strong opinion either way. The genesis is simply the test in b/188956438 breaking. I am not aware of anything else broken because of this, but I suspect it could be causing unnoticed issues. I agree that reintroducing cros_ec_cmd_xfer would effectively fix this issue (option 2 above).\n\nGuenter, do you have a preference?",
      "parentUuid": "112c4a51_292fc99d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 202,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3ccd1b2f34b5769eafb1b489e9cb6ea9edf728da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6cf52b9b_15c692ca",
        "filename": "util/comm-dev.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146659
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-13T16:13:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reverting 0d080459e813 would break all in-kernel users depending on it, so all callers of cros_ec_cmd_xfer_status() would have to be examined and updated accordingly. I personally don\u0027t think that would be a good idea.\nIt would make more sense to re-introduce cros_ec_cmd_xfer() and specifically use it for ioctls. In this context, note that cros_ec_cmd_xfer_status() is currently wrong anyway - it ignores errors from send_command() and instead uses cros_ec_map_error() to determine error codes from the EC. It should return immediately if send_command() fails, and not try to map anything.",
      "parentUuid": "f3bd69a0_6fd96970",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 202,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3ccd1b2f34b5769eafb1b489e9cb6ea9edf728da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "575013c1_2506e34d",
        "filename": "util/comm-dev.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132414
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-13T16:52:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Reverting 0d080459e813 would break all in-kernel users depending on it\n\nI said \"partially\" -- I think your test CL is what I had in mind, if I could convince myself I had my head on straight. I think my head is on straight now. (I was really mixed up thinking 0d080459e813 was the problem at first.)\n\n\u003e In this context, note that cros_ec_cmd_xfer_status() is currently wrong anyway - it ignores errors from send_command() and instead uses cros_ec_map_error() to determine error codes from the EC. It should return immediately if send_command() fails, and not try to map anything.\n\nYep. We\u0027re probably lucky that all users will pre-initialize the message struct to all-zero, and so an untouched -\u003eresult field still maps to 0 (and so we ignore it).",
      "parentUuid": "6cf52b9b_15c692ca",
      "range": {
